{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Order the systems of a schedule, run them only when a condition holds, and find out how a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule runs them.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lists the systems of one frame or step. When it runs, it decides the order from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"what you wrote and the constraints you added, and it runs the systems that can’t affect one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another at the same time."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Order-Systems","type":"heading","text":"Order Systems"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order you write them, adjusted by ordering constraints. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" moves a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system after another, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" moves it before one; every other system keeps its written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"place. A constraint that names a type with no system in the schedule is ignored. Constraints that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"form a cycle trap, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":" instead, for systems"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or constraints that come from configuration."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Run-Systems-Conditionally","type":"heading","text":"Run Systems Conditionally"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runIf(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" skips a system unless a condition on the world holds, such as the world holding no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Paused"},{"type":"text","text":" resource. On a nested schedule, it applies to each of the nested schedule’s systems. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system checks its conditions at the start of the wave it runs in, so a system that changes what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a condition reads affects the systems in later waves. A condition must read only what each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s access lists."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Understand-Waves","type":"heading","text":"Understand Waves"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two systems "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"conflict","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" when one writes a type the other reads or writes, or when either has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs the systems in "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"waves"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":": each wave holds the systems"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose earlier conflicting and ordered systems have run, and its systems run at the same time. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"commands systems queue apply when their wave finishes, so a system in the same wave doesn’t see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another’s spawns, despawns or inserts. To see them, order it after the system that queued them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The world ends as though the systems had run one after another, in order. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runSerially(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runs the same waves one system at a time, with the same result. Use it to step through a system in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a debugger, or to rule out running at the same time as the cause of a problem."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A system’s access comes from its parameters, with the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()"},{"text":" macro, or from an ","type":"text"},{"code":"access","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you declare by hand. A system without one may change anything, so it runs alone. In debug","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"builds, a system that reaches a type its access doesn’t list traps, so run a schedule’s tests in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"debug.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Find-Unordered-Conflicts","type":"heading","text":"Find Unordered Conflicts"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, the order they run in rests only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on how they happen to be written, which a later edit can change by accident.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" lists those pairs. Order each pair, or mark it with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem\/ambiguous(with:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" when either order is right, and check in a test that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list stays empty.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Group-Systems-into-Sets","type":"heading","text":"Group Systems into Sets"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" names a group of systems, so a constraint can refer to all of them at once."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Declare one as an empty enumeration. A system joins it with "},{"code":"inSet(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a nested schedule"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes "},{"code":"inSet(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"after(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"before(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"runIf(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for all of its systems. Every system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type is a set too, holding each system of that type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following schedule groups gravity and movement into a physics set that doesn’t run while","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the game is paused, and scores after every physics system:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Schedule {","        Gravity()","        Movement().after(Gravity.self)","    }","    .inSet(Physics.self)","    .runIf { world in !world.resources.contains(Paused.self) }","    Scoring().after(Physics.self)","}","print(frame.names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\", \"Scoring\"]\"","print(frame.ambiguities().isEmpty)","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Profile-a-Schedule","type":"heading","text":"Profile a Schedule"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Insert a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" resource into a world, and every schedule that runs on it records each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s runs and times. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/writeDOT(to:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" writes a schedule’s dependency graph in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"DOT language, so Graphviz can draw why systems run in the order they do and which can run at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same time.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/schedulingsystems"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"],"generated":true,"title":"Essentials"}],"metadata":{"title":"Scheduling Systems","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}]},"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduledSystem/ambiguous(with:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem\/ambiguous(with:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/scheduledsystem\/ambiguous(with:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns this system, also free to run in either order with every system in each of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"given sets."}],"title":"ambiguous(with:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguous","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<each ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"with"},{"kind":"text","text":": repeat (each "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":").Type) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScheduledSystem","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems15ScheduledSystemV"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"title":"Systems","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/run(on:)":{"title":"run(on:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs each system once on a world, running systems that don’t depend on each other at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same time."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/run(on:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"run","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"on","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order satisfies them all.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"}],"title":"CyclicOrdering","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"defaultImplementations":1,"required":true,"kind":"symbol","title":"access","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if it may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change anything."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"access","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Access","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"title":"ambiguities()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV","text":"Ambiguity"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","abstract":[{"text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"orders.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"System()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DeclaringSystems":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","type":"topic","title":"Declaring Systems","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemSet":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that names a group of systems, so ordering constraints can refer to all of them at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemset","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemSet"}],"title":"SystemSet","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemSet"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"title":"Schedule","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"title":"System","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/init(checked:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/init(checked:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a schedule of the given systems, throwing an error if their ordering constraints","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"form a cycle.","type":"text"}],"title":"init(checked:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"checked"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems15ScheduledSystemV","text":"ScheduledSystem","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems14CyclicOrderingV","text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/runSerially(on:)":{"title":"runSerially(on:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/runserially(on:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runSerially(on:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"runSerially","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"on","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":